From d289f5be3832c861a53ce944bf2543b40d4d947c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PromethenDev <PromethenDev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 17:32:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 47/97] graphics: display pacing statistics; opt-in guest
 vblank on the host display vblank

display_pacing_stats (Windows): a thread waits on the host display's vblanks (DXGI output of the window's
monitor) and logs per second how many new guest frames were presented before each one: 0 = the display
repeated a frame, 1 = even, 2+ = a frame was replaced before it was shown. A steady 60 flips/s does not show
this. The presenter counts successful presents and logs the Vulkan present mode it selected.

vsync_host_display (default off, experiment): guest vblanks fire on the host display's vblanks (every Nth at
N x 60 Hz) instead of the free-running timer, to stop phase drift between guest presents and the panel's
refresh. Falls back to the timer for non-multiple rates, failed or implausibly fast waits, and waits longer than
four periods (then for 5 s). Escalation review (GPT-6 Sol): unproven on a hybrid iGPU-display laptop, so opt-in
and judged by the pacing statistics.

Wine gates PASS (normal; keep-60 with the experiment on - no DXGI display under Wine, timer fallback).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
